  "ownership": "Control owns one bounded original pending Request/deadline and the original AsyncFd. Admission validates the budget before socket allocation. Cancellation retains pending request, sent bit and absolute deadline; expiry fails the channel without issuing another request or creating a quiescence receipt. Original child lease retains endpoint through native settlement. Existing supervisor cleanup owns original child/stdout/encoder retirement; timeout alone neither releases nor reuses those resources. Fresh helper admission remains behind original cleanup. No new native allocation, task, callback cycle or retained frame is added.",
  "bounds": "Host default 2000 ms, valid 1..60000 ms, read at channel attachment. Common Duration contract >0 and <=60 seconds. One pending/completed request and one immutable budget per Control.",
  "scope": "Private helper processes and real socket control; C helper sanitizer fixture with fake EVDI. No physical display/lock event acceptance or unrestricted native safety claim. Installed sessions and binaries untouched."
